<http://data.silknow.org/object/11554240-92dd-3ab5-bbc0-29ac1df0da1e>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Satin bonnet trimmed with a striped satin ribbon, England, 1840-1845"@en , "Black satin bonnet trimmed with a black striped satin ribbon, and a black looped braid around the outside of the brim. Cottage shaped, made in one piece with the crown and brim in one. Drawn bonnet made by gathering the satin over strips of stiffening, possibly whalebone or cane. The crown (calotte) is plain and the brim is trimmed with two narrow bands of narrow pleating. The bavolet is of satin with a satin piping and lined with spotted silk net. Trimmed with a twisted satin drape around the crown through which is draped the twisting satin trimming. This is arranged in a bow at the centre back and descending loops of ribbon on the right side of the head. The ties are of black ribbed silk ribbon with a purl edge. The head lining is of black silk through which is threaded a brown draw cord. The entire bonnet is interlined with white stiffened linen to which are stitched stiffening wires. The bonnet is well and neatly made, sober and conventional in style."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/d2d245e3-a126-3308-8117-213a428e8c19> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Satin bonnet trimmed with a striped satin ribbon, England, 1840-1845"@en , "Black satin bonnet trimmed with a black striped satin ribbon, and a black looped braid around the outside of the brim. Cottage shaped, made in one piece with the crown and brim in one. Drawn bonnet made by gathering the satin over strips of stiffening, possibly whalebone or cane. The crown (calotte) is plain and the brim is trimmed with two narrow bands of narrow pleating. The bavolet is of satin with a satin piping and lined with spotted silk net. Trimmed with a twisted satin drape around the crown through which is draped the twisting satin trimming. This is arranged in a bow at the centre back and descending loops of ribbon on the right side of the head. The ties are of black ribbed silk ribbon with a purl edge. The head lining is of black silk through which is threaded a brown draw cord. The entire bonnet is interlined with white stiffened linen to which are stitched stiffening wires. The bonnet is well and neatly made, sober and conventional in style."@en ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.27-1984" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O355880> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/11554240-92dd-3ab5-bbc0-29ac1df0da1e/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
